  "question": {
    "text": "The electrostatic force $\\left(\\overrightarrow{F_1}\\right)$ and magnetic force $\\left(\\vec{F}_2\\right)$ acting on a charge $q$ moving with velocity $v$ can be written :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "M9pQs",
      "text": "$\\vec{F}_1=q \\vec{E}, \\vec{F}_2=q(\\vec{V} \\times \\vec{B})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "yYUrN",
      "text": "$\\vec{F}_1=q \\vec{B}, \\vec{F}_2=q(\\vec{B} \\times \\vec{V})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ohUI3",
      "text": "$\\vec{F}_1=q \\vec{E}, \\vec{F}_2=q(\\vec{B} \\times \\vec{V})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pDAVm",
      "text": "$\\vec{F}_1=q \\vec{V} \\cdot \\vec{E}, \\vec{F}_2=q(\\vec{B} \\cdot \\vec{V})$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_1=\\mathrm{q} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{E}} \\\\\n& \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_2=\\mathrm{q}(\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{V}} \\times \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}})\n\\end{aligned}$\n(Theory)",
